model_answer_en:
CSS (Cascading Style Sheets): a style language used to describe the presentation (look and formatting) of HTML documents. CSS separates content (HTML structure) from presentation (visual styling).

Why CSS is used in web design:
1. Separation of concerns: HTML defines structure, CSS defines appearance — cleaner code
2. Reusability: one CSS file can style an entire website
3. Maintainability: change one CSS rule to update all matching elements
4. Responsive design: media queries adapt layout to different screen sizes
5. Faster load times: external CSS is cached by browsers

CSS code:
p {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: blue;
  font-size: 16px;
}

